  "goodToKnow": "Die Kathedrale is a cathedral, strictly a church with a bishop's seat (Latin cathedra). In Germany, cathedrals are usually called der Dom (Kölner Dom, Berliner Dom, which isn't even a bishop's seat) or das Münster (Ulmer Münster, with the world's tallest church spire, 161.5 metres). Kathedrale is used more for foreign cathedrals: die Kathedrale von Chartres. Plural: die Kathedralen."
